\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou to whom the sick and dying
\par Ever came, nor came in vain,
\par Still with healing words replying
\par To the wearied cry of pain,
\par Hear us, Jesu, as we meet,
\par Suppliants at Thy mercy- seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Every care, and every sorrow, 
\par Be it great, or be it small,
\par Yesterday, to-day, to- morrow,
\par When, where'er it may befall,
\par Lay we  humbly at Thy feet,
\par Suppliants at Thy mercy- seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Still the weary, sick, and dying
\par Need a brother's, sister's care;
\par On Thy higher help relying,
\par May we now their burden share,
\par Bringing all our offerings meet,
\par Suppliants at Thy mercy- seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. May each child of Thine be willing,
\par Willing both in hand and heart,
\par All the law of love fulfilling,
\par Ever comfort to impart,
\par Ever bringing offerings meet,
\par Suppliants to Thy mercy- seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So may sickness, sin, and sadness
\par To Thy healing power yield,
\par Till the sick and sad, in gladness,
\par Rescued, ransomed, cleansed, healed,
\par One in Thee together meet,
\par Pardoned at Thy judgement- seat.
\par                                        Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

